PHP 8.6 removed the INI_INT() macro (use zend_ini_long_literal()) and the
ZEND_PARSE_PARAMS_THROW flag together with the *_throw() parameter parsers,
since ZPP always throws (UPGRADING.INTERNALS). No upstream fix exists as of
2026-11-19 (php-decimal/ext-decimal master still uses both); the changes are
guarded so older PHP keeps the old spelling. Drop once upstream ships the
equivalent.

diff --git a/php_decimal.c b/php_decimal.c
index 6456009..02e8bf4 100644
--- a/php_decimal.c
+++ b/php_decimal.c
@@ -67,7 +67,11 @@ static void php_decimal_mpd_free(void *ptr)
  */
 static void php_decimal_disable_opcache_pass2()
 {
+#if PHP_VERSION_ID >= 80600
+    zend_long level = zend_ini_long_literal("opcache.optimization_level");
+#else
     zend_long level = INI_INT("opcache.optimization_level");
+#endif
 
     if (level & 2) {
         zend_string *key = zend_string_init(ZEND_STRL("opcache.optimization_level"), 1);
